From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:51:19 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: macsmc: hold the charge with CHLS
 where CHTE and CH0C are absent

The SMC firmware of the M4 Pro MacBook Pros has neither CHTE nor CH0C
(and no CH0I), so charge_behaviour offers no inhibit-charge and no
force-discharge there. It has the CHLS charge limit word and the CH0J
inflow key.

- inhibit-charge: where neither CHTE nor CH0C exists, set CHLS to the
  current charge (clamped to 10-99 %) with CHLS_HOLD (bit 9: hold at the
  limit instead of charging through to full) and no drain. The user's
  own limit is kept while the hold lasts: the end threshold still reads
  and sets it, and auto or auto-discharge writes it back.
- force-discharge: where CH0I is absent, write 1 to CH0J to cut the
  external power inflow; 0 restores it. CH0J is a command key, so the
  state is read from CH0R bit 5.

Macs with CHTE or CH0C keep their inhibit key, and bit 9 is left alone
there. KUnit covers the hold, the restore of the user's limit, the
CHTE precedence and CH0J.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
(cherry picked from commit 0a6b4f118955491341deace3ed4a04101246cf48)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
